{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-4019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-4019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}} \\\\ {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =2x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {y}^{2}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 2x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{3}}{3} & ={x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ {y}^{3} & =3{x}^{2}+3{C}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+C,\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}$  is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{13})}^{3} & =3(2)^{2}+C \\\\ 13 & =12+C \\\\ C & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2x}{{y}^{2}}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$ is\n\n$$\n{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-4019" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-4019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-4019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+1"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{2}-1"] ["math" "{y}^{3}=\\frac{1}{6}{x}^{2}+1"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+1"] ["math" "{y}^{3}={x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-4019" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{y}^{3}=3{x}^{2}+1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-8309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation ${y}^{′}=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)}$ that satisfies $y(0)=0.$ Assume that $-\\frac{\\pi }{4}<y<\\frac{\\pi }{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-8309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)}{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)} \\\\ (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x) \\\\ \\int (\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y))\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2y)\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${C}_{1}=2C.$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=0$ to find ${C}_{1}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2\\cdot 0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3\\cdot 0)+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =-\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 1+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y) & =\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x) \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we can write the above equation as\n\n$$\n3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-8309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-8309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-8309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)"] ["math" "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))"] ["math" "5\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-8309" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "3\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2y)=2(1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x))"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y}$ that satisfies $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡y} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =x+C \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡y & =-x-C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=\\frac{\\pi }{2}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2}) & =-0-C \\\\ 0 & =0-C \\\\ C & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡2y=-2x+1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=x+1"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=-2x"] ["math" "\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=x"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104055" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡y=-x"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies $y(1)=1.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-{y}^{2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =1 \\\\ -\\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{y} & =x+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{x+C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe conclude that the general solution is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x+C},\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{1}{1+C} \\\\ 1+C & =1 \\\\ C & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+{y}^{2}=0$ that satisfies the condition $y(1)=1$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{x}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2-x}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{2x-1}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{1}{x}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x+1}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{x}-1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-50220" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\frac{1}{x}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation\n$\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4x\\sqrt{y}$\nthat satisfies the condition $y(1)=9.$  Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find the particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x\\sqrt{y} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{y}}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 2\\sqrt{y} & =2{x}^{2}+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\sqrt{y} & ={x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2} \\\\ y & ={({x}^{2}+\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2})}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAssuming $y>0,$ the general solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+C)^{2},\n$$\n\nwhere $C=\\frac{{C}_{1}}{2}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(1)=9$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9 & =((1)^{2}+C)^{2} \\\\ 9 & =(1+C)^{2} \\\\ 3 & =1+C \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=({x}^{2}+2)^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355528" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "(x^2+2)^2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x}=3$ that satisfies $y(1)=11.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x\\sqrt{x} & =3 \\\\ \\sqrt{x}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3+4x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\text{d}y & =(3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\text{d}y & =\\int (3{x}^{-1/2}+4x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ y & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(1)=11$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(1) & =11 \\\\ 6(1)^{1/2}+2(1)^{2}+C & =11 \\\\ C+8 & =11 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(x) & =6{x}^{1/2}+2{x}^{2}+3 \\\\  & =6\\sqrt{x}+2{x}^{2}+3.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-355547" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355547" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "2x^2+6\\sqrt{x}+3"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2}=4x$ that satisfies $y(0)=1.$ Assume that $y>0.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-4x{y}^{2} & =4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x{y}^{2}+4x \\\\ 2y\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =4x({y}^{2}+1) \\\\ \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{2y}{{y}^{2}+1}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int 4x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1) & =2{x}^{2}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExponentiating both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({y}^{2}+1)} & ={e}^{2{x}^{2}+C} \\\\ {y}^{2}+1 & =C{e}^{2{x}^{2}} \\\\ y & =\\sqrt{C{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere we used that $y>0.$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(0)=1$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C{e}^{2(0)^{2}}-1} & =1 \\\\ \\sqrt{C-1} & =1 \\\\ C-1 & =1 \\\\ C & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, the particular solution is\n\n$$\ny(x)=\\sqrt{2{e}^{2{x}^{2}}-1}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355559" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-355559" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355559" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\sqrt{2e^{2x^2}-1}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={y}^{2}(3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}) \\\\ \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3} \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (3{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{{y}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}y & =3\\int {x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x-4\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -\\frac{1}{y} & ={x}^{3}-{x}^{4}+C \\\\ y & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}-C}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the initial condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(2) & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{{2}^{4}-{2}^{3}-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ \\frac{1}{8-C} & =\\frac{1}{8} \\\\ C & =0\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=3{y}^{2}{x}^{2}-4{y}^{2}{x}^{3}$ that satisfies the condition $y(2)=\\frac{1}{8}$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\frac{1}{{x}^{4}-{x}^{3}}\\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-104064" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{1}