ln}⁡({e}^{-y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{x}+C) \\\\ -y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}) \\\\ y & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{x}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ -\\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-{e}^{0}) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡2 \\\\ C-1 & =2 \\\\ C & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{x+y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡2$ is\n\n$$\ny=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-14267" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-14267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-14267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+x+{e}^{x})"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1+{e}^{x})"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-2x-{e}^{x})"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x})"] ["math" "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+{e}^{x})"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-14267" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3-{e}^{x})"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the specific solution to the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ given that $\\,y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4.$\n\n$y(x)=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x-y} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x}{e}^{-y} \\\\ {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & ={e}^{-x} \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int {e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =\\int {e}^{-x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ {e}^{y} & =-{e}^{-x}+C\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the natural logarithm to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({e}^{y}) & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{-x}+C).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now apply the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ to find $C:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(-{e}^{0}+C) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡(C-1) & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4 \\\\ C-1 & =\\frac{1}{4} \\\\ C & =\\frac{5}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}={e}^{-x-y}$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=-\\operatorname{ln}⁡4$ is\n\n$$\ny=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{5}{4}-{e}^{-x}).\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "afe84ab9c69899a72f3968d99750212c45d5146749e48d0ceaee86452fb5b9aa"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "q-355577" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ln(\\frac{5}{4}-e^{-x})"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/state.json" "file_sha256" "5fa6b99adc2df0ab978070eb1adc0626a2b7c90435331591b9315d3f6a3d1106"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32"} {"question" "e-540" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5y \\\\ \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =5 \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\frac{1}{y}\\,\\text{d}y & =5\\int \\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\operatorname{ln}⁡|y| & =5x+C\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\pm {e}^{5x+C} \\\\  & =\\pm {e}^{C}{e}^{5x} \\\\  & =K{e}^{5x}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant. \n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(0) & =3 \\\\ K{e}^{5\\cdot 0} & =3 \\\\ K & =3\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x}  \\,.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-540.json" "file_sha256" "1a22bc19e61aacd899d91e4ef567556882bdb4398e2c495b8915566861d8da32"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that  $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0.$ Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6} .$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312"} {"question" "e-541" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x) \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(3y)\\,\\text{d}y & =-\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+C \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3y) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)+{C}_{1}\\,,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C.$\n\nNow let's apply the condition $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$ to find $C_1\\mathbin{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(3\\cdot 0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4})+{C}_{1} \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(0) & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})+{C}_{1} \\\\ 0 & =0+{C}_{1} \\\\ {C}_{1} & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y)   =  \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14013233/example-541.json" "file_sha256" "a5f3e5f03f387c5a545cbc855fc0d68f5d920decc385e2d02bac45f56f99b312"}] "usage" {"e-541" [] "q-4019" [] "e-540" []} "basis" 1163 "retractions" [[17592186101309 :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\frac{dy}{dx} = \\frac{2x}{y^{2}}$ that satisfies $y(2) = \\sqrt[3]{13}$."] [17592186101309 :question/worked-solution "Separate and integrate:\n$$y^2\\,dy=2x\\,dx,\\qquad \\frac{y^3}{3}=x^2+C.$$\nWrite $y^3=3x^2+K$ and apply $y(2)=\\sqrt[3]{13}$:\n$$13=12+K,\\qquad K=1.$$\nTherefore $y^3=3x^2+1$, or $y=\\sqrt[3]{3x^2+1}$."] [17592186101309 :question/difficulty 17592186045465] [17592186100642 :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $y' = 5y$ that satisfies $y(0)=3$."] [17592186100642 :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\frac{dy}{dx} &= 5y \\\\\n\\frac{1}{y}\\frac{dy}{dx} &= 5 \\\\\n\\int \\frac{1}{y}\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= 5\\int dx \\\\\n\\int \\frac{1}{y}dy &= 5\\int dx \\\\\n\\ln \\mid y \\mid &= 5x + C\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nApplying the exponential function to both sides, we find the general solution:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny &= \\pm  e^{5x + C} \\\\\n&= \\pm  e^{C}e^{5x} \\\\\n&= Ke^{5x}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $K=\\pm e^{C}$ is an arbitrary constant.\n\nNow we apply the condition $y(0) = 3$ to find $K$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny(0) &= 3 \\\\\nKe^{5 \\cdot 0} &= 3 \\\\\nK &= 3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus the particular solution of $y' = 5y$ that satisfies the condition $y(0)=3$ is\n\n$$\ny = 3 e^{5x} \\,\n$$"] [17592186100646 :question/problem "Find the particular solution to the differential equation $\\cos(3y)\\dfrac {\\textrm{d}y} {\\textrm{d}x} + \\sin(2x) = 0$ given that $y\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0$. Assume that $-\\dfrac{\\pi}{6} < y < \\dfrac{\\pi}{6}$."] [17592186100646 :question/worked-solution "We first find the general solution, and then apply the given initial condition to find a particular solution.\n\nSeparating variables and integrating both sides with respect to $x$, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\cos (3y)\\frac{dy}{dx} &= -\\sin (2x) \\\\\n\\int \\cos (3y)\\frac{dy}{dx}dx &= - \\int \\sin (2x)dx \\\\\n\\int \\cos (3y)dy &= - \\int \\sin (2x)dx \\\\\n\\frac{1}{3}\\sin (3y) &= \\frac{1}{2}\\cos (2x) + C \\\\\n\\sin (3y) &= \\frac{3}{2}\\cos (2x) + C_{1}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C_1=3C$.\n\nNow let's apply the condition\n\n$$\ny\\left(\\dfrac{\\pi}{4}\\right) = 0\n$$\n\nto find $C_1$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\ny(\\frac{\\pi }{4}) &= 0 \\\\\n\\sin (3 \\cdot 0) &= \\frac{3}{2}\\cos (2 \\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{4}) + C_{1} \\\\\n\\sin (0) &= \\frac{3}{2}\\cos (\\frac{\\pi }{2}) + C_{1} \\\\\n0 &= 0 + C_{1} \\\\\nC_{1} &= 0\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo we get the particular solution in implicit form:\n\n$$\n\\sin(3y) = \\dfrac {3} {2} \\cos(2x)\n$$"]] "immutable_answers" [17592186099451 17592186099452 17592186099453 17592186099454 17592186099455] "immutable_fields" [[17592186099450 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099450 :answer-field/id] [17592186099450 :answer-field/key] [17592186099450 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
